on in the Plasmodium vivax merozoite surface protein 1 gene among Indian and Colombian isolates</article-title><source>Malar J</source><year>2004</year><volume>3</volume><fpage>4</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15003129</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1186/1475-2875-3-4</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Imwong</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Nair</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Pukrittayakamee</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Sudimack</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Williams</surname><given-names>JT</given-names></name><name><surname>Mayxay</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Newton</surname><given-names>PN</given-names></name><name><surname>Kim</surname><given-names>JR</given-names></name><name><surname>Nandy</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Osorio</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Carlton</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>White</surname><given-names>NJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Day</surname><given-names>NP</given-names></name><name><surname>Anderson</surname><given-names>TJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Contrasting genetic structure in Plasmodium vivax populations from Asia and South America</article-title><source>Int J Parasitol</source><year>2007</year><volume>37</volume><fpage>1013</fpage><lpage>1022</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17442318</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.ijpara.2007.02.010</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cui</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Escalante</surname><given-names>AA</given-names></name><name><surname>Imwong</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Sno